WEBVTT

00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:07.180
<i>I don't remember much about 
how I sang at that time.</i>

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.020
<i>I've made up my mind.</i>

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.910
<i>I will definitely make you look my way.</i>

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.160
<i>Fly!</i>

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:32.300
<i>Whether I'm awake or asleep</i>

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.720
<i>I'm nothing more than a canary</i>

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:39.630
<i>Inside a sweet, glistening cage of ideals</i>

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:42.630
<i>Whether I'm awake or asleep</i>

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:43.460
<i>This is bad. Alice is going berserk again.</i>

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:44.770
<i>I can't leave my cage</i>

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:50.010
<i>I'm always there when I wake up</i>

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:47.770
<i>It's okay.</i>

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:51.950
<i>I can keep up.</i>

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:55.840
<i>You say that's fine if everyone's here</i>

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:56.280
<i>Really, our little canary is going wild.</i>

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:59.910
<i>So come here with me</i>

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:59.070
<i>We'll catch you this time, though!</i>

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:03.240
<i>She's rushing even more than 
at the school performance.</i>

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:06.210
<i>When I shout, that alone makes me invincible</i>

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:06.620
<i>But unlike then, she's 
listening to us this time.</i>

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:10.320
<i>So please don't open this cage</i>

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:07.900
<i>This...</i>

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:10.620
<i>might work!</i>

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:15.020
<i>I'll fall</i>

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:21.160
<i>Straight down</i>

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:23.150
<i>It's not enough.</i>

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:24.700
<i>Not enough! Not enough!</i>

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:26.290
<i>I won't reach him like this!</i>

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:28.390
<i>More.</i>

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:29.690
<i>More.</i>

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:32.190
<i>More!</i>

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:38.750
Hey... Momo, what are you doing?

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:39.700
Is your guitar okay?

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:45.330
Momo?

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:47.150
Nino.

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:52.340
<i>What is this?</i>

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:00.140
<i>She's a monster.</i>

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:05.460
<i>Even if I'm completely naked, 
I'm not scared anymore</i>

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:09.380
<i>I'll keep on singing, because I'm a canary</i>

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.000
TV Prep Room A

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:31.920
♭06 Today and Tomorrow, We'll Walk

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:37.510
Score!

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:42.020
The single's going to sell for sure!

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:42.390
We definitely made her 
berserking work for us!

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:45.430
Man, that seriously felt amazing!

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:51.620
Did I...

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:57.190
Did I really sing all right?

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:00.700
You did.

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:04.190
<i>On that big, open stage,</i>

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:07.240
<i>singing my heart out with the lights on me...</i>

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:12.220
<i>I could almost see ahead of me.</i>

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:17.710
You let me sing.

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:20.720
Thank you.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:26.790
I can't make money with your song.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:31.060
<i>I don't know how Momo 
spent the last six years.</i>

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:34.160
I didn't sing all this time for that!

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:39.550
<i>I didn't know a thing. 
I was only thinking of myself.</i>

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:42.740
<i>All I could do was thrust 
myself upon him with words.</i>

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:45.230
<i>Momo, I'm sorry.</i>

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:49.990
<i>I should have sung all my 
feelings to you right then.</i>

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:54.460
<i>Even if they wouldn't reach your heart.</i>

00:03:57.460 --> 00:04:00.010
Did you see yesterday's <i>Music King</i>?

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:01.480
I saw it!

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:03.770
In NO Hurry was totally awesome!

00:04:03.770 --> 00:04:05.140
Right?

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:07.460
TV is amazing.

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:10.140
I heard the same conversation 
so many times at the station.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:11.640
Now that you mention it,

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:15.000
we hadn't even heard that they'd decided 
on the first album's release date.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:16.700
So it seems.

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:19.800
That Yana! He never tells us anything.

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:21.290
He's so mean!

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:26.160
My mother's been so moved 
ever since last night.

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:29.140
My little girl's on TV!

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.140
She hasn't stopped crying.

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:35.880
Didn't In NO Hurry seem different 
from their CDs last night?

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:37.040
Did they?

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:39.070
I thought they were great live.

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:42.560
Looks like we'll be hearing more of them.

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:44.250
They made their TV debut, after all.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:46.300
I totally can't wait.

00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:52.940
Amazing. There are tons of rips online.

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:53.890
Seriously?

00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:55.220
Dead serious.

00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:56.200
Dead...

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:01.370
Hello.

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:02.760
<i>Arisugawa-san?</i>

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:05.580
<i>I'm Kuze from Möbius Music.</i>

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:09.500
<i>Sorry to bring this up out of the blue, but...</i>

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:13.730
In NO Hurry was so great yesterday.

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:15.360
They're releasing an album, right?

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:16.870
I'm totally gonna buy it!

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:25.530
Hello, Arisugawa-san.

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:27.970
Sorry to call you out here so suddenly.

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:30.950
It's too bad about the audition.

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:35.180
I was one of the judges. 
Do you remember seeing me?

00:05:35.450 --> 00:05:39.440
No. Um, why exactly did you invite me here?

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:41.510
Here. This is for you.

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:42.780
It's Momo's guitar.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:43.440
Huh?

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:46.450
It got scratched, so he said 
he wanted to throw it out.

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:50.500
So I made the decision to give it to you.

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:52.950
Huh? Wh-Why me?

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:55.640
Because Momo was badly shaken.

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:58.870
When he heard you sing 
on <i>Music King</i>, I mean.

00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:02.800
Oh, don't worry.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.380
I won't tell anyone.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:08.100
Momo's the only one who figured out 
you were Alice from In NO Hurry.

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:10.240
Look at this scratch.

00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:14.600
Momo dropped his mug here 
while listening to you sing.

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:18.900
It wasn't about money.

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:21.730
He just couldn't stop himself from reacting.

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:24.110
I want you to have it.

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:26.400
Because it's proof that,

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:29.490
for an instant, your voice
managed to move his heart.

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:31.830
Take care of it.

00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:38.790
Guitar!

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:41.820
Guitar!

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:45.050
What's gotten into you, Alice?

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:45.790
Guitar!

00:06:45.790 --> 00:06:46.630
Huh?

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:48.010
Guitar!

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:52.260
Uh, I know that's a guitar. What about it?

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:54.100
Guitar!

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:56.100
Are you even listening?

00:06:57.240 --> 00:06:58.430
It's Momo's guitar.

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:04.030
Apparently, Momo figured out that 
it was me on yesterday's <i>Music King</i>.

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:06.750
He was so shaken when he heard me sing

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:09.360
that he dropped his mug on his guitar.

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:13.820
And this is that guitar. Someone 
from Möbius said I could have it.

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:15.690
Momo...

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:20.040
It's all thanks to you.

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:22.170
Thank you.

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:25.320
It's all because you made me into Alice.

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:29.610
Because you let me sing with In NO Hurry.

00:07:30.710 --> 00:07:33.680
That's why I could reach Momo, 
even if only a little.

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:38.970
This scratch is tiny, 
but it makes me so happy.

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:43.480
Just so, so, so happy.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:47.360
I wanted to tell you before anyone else.

00:07:48.350 --> 00:07:51.740
<i>I feel like, in the six years since 
I let go of Momo's hand,</i>

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:55.870
<i>this is the first time I've touched him.</i>

00:07:56.850 --> 00:08:01.370
<i>Even if it's just a tiny scratch,
only a few centimeters long.</i>

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:03.870
<i>I'll sing.</i>

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:10.010
<i>Next time I see Momo, I'll show 
him even more of how I feel.</i>

00:08:11.570 --> 00:08:13.190
<i>Until it reaches him.</i>

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:15.770
<i>Until he looks my way.</i>

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:21.970
I don't mind teaching you how to play guitar.

00:08:21.970 --> 00:08:23.730
Really? I'm so happy!

00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:26.630
Then I want to play one of your songs!

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:31.320
I like your songs best.

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:33.080
I love them!

00:08:39.170 --> 00:08:42.770
Then I guess I could teach you "Canary."

00:08:43.230 --> 00:08:43.960
Sure!

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:48.340
You gave Nino my guitar?

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:50.710
Why did you do that without asking?

00:08:51.140 --> 00:08:53.720
I also told her about how 
you were so shaken.

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:57.740
Because you seemed to really regret

00:08:57.740 --> 00:08:59.970
what happened on the day of the audition.

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:04.100
She was probably relieved to know 
that might not be how you really felt.

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:07.480
Just because you feel you owe someone

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:09.610
doesn't mean you have to push them away.

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:11.870
You're so unfair.

00:09:11.870 --> 00:09:14.510
What you should be calling 
me is "wise," Momo-chan.

00:09:14.510 --> 00:09:16.860
Please don't treat me like a child.

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:19.450
But you are a child.

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:22.160
I'll be back on Saturday.

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:24.370
Make sure you lock up.

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:52.570
Great!

00:09:52.570 --> 00:09:54.670
You were so awful at first that I was worried,

00:09:54.670 --> 00:09:56.780
but you somehow managed 
to get the intro down!

00:09:55.370 --> 00:10:00.640
Yuzu! I'm a genius!

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:01.140
Yep! You're not listening again today!

00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:02.280
Nice positivity!

00:10:05.530 --> 00:10:06.620
<i>I'm so happy!</i>

00:10:07.230 --> 00:10:09.610
<i>I'm singing with Momo's guitar!</i>

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:15.500
What? Arisugawa, you can play the guitar?

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:16.280
Baldy.

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:17.240
Baldy?!

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:19.650
He's Baldy. We went to 
elementary school together.

00:10:19.650 --> 00:10:20.870
He went bald a long time ago.

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:22.420
I did not go bald!

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:24.060
It's been awhile, Baldy.

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:26.060
Are you listening to me?!

00:10:26.820 --> 00:10:28.580
Arisugawa-san, you play the guitar?

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:30.620
Hey, that's a Greco. Sweet.

00:10:30.620 --> 00:10:31.940
Play something!

00:10:32.330 --> 00:10:34.890
I've only just started learning.

00:10:35.370 --> 00:10:37.820
When I learn a song, I'll play it for you.

00:10:39.870 --> 00:10:44.310
I thought Arisugawa-san was just some 
weird girl in a mask and headphones.

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:46.720
But she's actually pretty cute!

00:10:46.720 --> 00:10:48.040
Yeah, I guess.

00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:51.860
I think I've finally gotten F down.

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:53.490
What's going on there?

00:10:53.490 --> 00:10:57.320
She got a guitar, so Yuzu's been 
teaching her every morning.

00:10:57.320 --> 00:11:00.590
You know... Since the <i>Music King</i> 
thing went better than expected,

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:02.550
we've got some free time.

00:11:02.550 --> 00:11:04.780
Yana-chan wants to keep 
the fans "hungry," he says,

00:11:04.780 --> 00:11:06.810
so he's not booking anything 
else until summer.

00:11:07.820 --> 00:11:08.720
I see.

00:11:10.150 --> 00:11:12.310
Why don't you just tell him?

00:11:12.310 --> 00:11:14.070
"Teach me, too."

00:11:14.070 --> 00:11:15.900
I can play guitar already!

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:18.690
Oh, no! I dropped my earring!

00:11:19.480 --> 00:11:20.400
Sheesh.

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:22.430
Here.

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:26.870
Thanks, Haruyoshi-senpai.

00:11:32.970 --> 00:11:34.340
What's with those earrings?

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:37.560
Yuzu gave them to her.

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:41.430
Haruyoshi, have you gotten Miou 
a birthday present yet?

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:43.060
I figured something out.

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:44.700
I got one, too.

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:48.920
You guys are fast! What should I get her?

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:53.480
Gifts for Ladies

00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:53.480
If I'm gonna buy her something, 
I want it to make her really happy.

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:03.270
How about some earrings?

00:12:03.270 --> 00:12:03.900
Huh?

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:07.180
Miou got her ears pierced last month.

00:12:07.180 --> 00:12:08.010
Did you know?

00:12:08.010 --> 00:12:10.290
I didn't! That's a great idea.

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:12.090
Thanks, Haruyoshi.

00:12:12.090 --> 00:12:12.750
Sure.

00:12:13.260 --> 00:12:15.560
I know what to do now. Earrings, huh?

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:17.220
I think she'd like these.

00:12:19.120 --> 00:12:22.880
You just can't get a break, 
huh, Haruyoshi-senpai?

00:12:23.100 --> 00:12:24.890
With what, Kuro?

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:27.290
Nothing at all.

00:12:29.490 --> 00:12:31.140
Arisugawa-san.

00:12:31.880 --> 00:12:34.920
I wanted you to know how 
grateful I am for the guitar.

00:12:35.740 --> 00:12:37.220
Thank you very much.

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:39.570
You didn't have to go out of your way.

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:41.150
Momo isn't even here.

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:43.180
Huh? No, I know that.

00:12:43.180 --> 00:12:45.800
More like, I never figured you'd 
let me meet him, anyway.

00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:48.010
If you've got a message 
for him, I can tell him.

00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:49.510
I don't, really.

00:12:49.510 --> 00:12:50.480
Are you sure?

00:12:50.480 --> 00:12:54.320
Well, if you think of something, 
you can tell me anytime.

00:12:54.320 --> 00:12:56.580
Here. My business card.

00:12:57.320 --> 00:12:59.590
After all, I live with him.

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:02.330
Later.

00:13:04.590 --> 00:13:07.820
Hase

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:14.850
<i>What is Kuze-san to Momo?</i>

00:13:15.650 --> 00:13:17.890
<i>She seems to know him really well.</i>

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:19.950
<i>Just what are they...</i>

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:21.230
Prick

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:23.740
Prick

00:13:24.110 --> 00:13:25.030
Huh?

00:13:25.030 --> 00:13:25.740
Prick

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:27.470
What's this?

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:27.740
Prick

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:30.530
<i>It hurts.</i>

00:13:40.430 --> 00:13:41.210
It hurts.

00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:51.180
Alice, are you sick?

00:13:51.770 --> 00:13:54.060
My chest has been hurting since yesterday.

00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:56.330
What's up with that? Go to the hospital.

00:13:57.840 --> 00:13:58.660
Yuzu.

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:02.590
If you lived with me, 
we'd be roommates, right?

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:06.860
Wh-Where'd this come from all of a sudden?

00:14:07.120 --> 00:14:11.130
Apparently, Momo is living with 
the woman who gave me this guitar.

00:14:12.670 --> 00:14:15.310
A boy and girl can live together as 
roommates, nothing romantic, right?

00:14:15.310 --> 00:14:16.370
Because they're friends.

00:14:17.570 --> 00:14:21.630
I've never once thought of you as a friend.

00:14:21.800 --> 00:14:22.630
Huh?

00:14:23.990 --> 00:14:25.290
Not a friend?

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:27.440
So what am I? An acquaintance? 
Just someone you know?

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:30.850
No, you're a friend! You're my friend, Alice!

00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:32.510
So we'd be roommates!

00:14:32.920 --> 00:14:34.000
You're right.

00:14:34.270 --> 00:14:35.740
Let's practice, Yuzu.

00:14:35.740 --> 00:14:36.520
Yeah.

00:14:40.090 --> 00:14:43.290
<i>That's right. They're just 
roommates, and nothing more.</i>

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:45.060
<i>It's nothing to be worried about.</i>

00:14:46.890 --> 00:14:48.940
<i>Nothing to worry about.</i>

00:14:50.050 --> 00:14:52.600
In NO Hurry Makes Waves with "Canary,"
Music Video and Album in the Works!

00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:53.540
In NO Hurry's TV Appearance Causes a Stir;
The Secret to Their Skyrocketing Popularity

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:55.680
Miou.

00:14:57.340 --> 00:14:58.820
Oh, Yuzu.

00:14:59.180 --> 00:15:00.950
You're as short as ever today.

00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:02.420
Are you picking a fight?

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:05.340
Uh, well..

00:15:05.650 --> 00:15:08.260
I passed the audition!

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:10.730
Seriously? Wow...

00:15:10.730 --> 00:15:12.210
You're amazing, Miou.

00:15:12.210 --> 00:15:13.260
Congratulations.

00:15:13.790 --> 00:15:15.760
We'd better not fall behind.

00:15:19.700 --> 00:15:21.650
I heard you're making an album.

00:15:21.870 --> 00:15:24.860
Yeah. I'm writing tons of songs right now.

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:25.950
Yeah?

00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:28.140
Yana's really into it, too.

00:15:28.140 --> 00:15:30.650
He says I need to have 
five songs by tomorrow.

00:15:30.650 --> 00:15:32.090
Really?

00:15:32.090 --> 00:15:32.790
Yeah.

00:15:33.350 --> 00:15:34.180
Later!

00:15:45.150 --> 00:15:46.000
Miou.

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:49.970
What's the matter? Not going home?

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:53.510
You sure have it good, don't you, Nino?

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:09.570
Hey.

00:16:09.930 --> 00:16:11.640
Why did you follow me?

00:16:11.640 --> 00:16:13.700
I want to be alone!

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:16.320
I just wanted to come here, too.

00:16:16.880 --> 00:16:19.080
Yuigahama is like my own backyard to me.

00:16:21.490 --> 00:16:23.840
I sing here every morning.

00:16:23.840 --> 00:16:26.640
And I always come here 
when I want to calm down.

00:16:29.970 --> 00:16:31.200
You make me so mad!

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:33.100
Wherever I go, everyone's talking about you.

00:16:33.980 --> 00:16:36.470
Why did you have to come 
back into Yuzu's life?

00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:39.430
In NO Hurry was where I belonged!

00:16:40.150 --> 00:16:42.050
I thought that if I left In NO Hurry,

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:44.420
joined another band,

00:16:44.420 --> 00:16:46.680
and In NO Hurry failed with 
you as my replacement,

00:16:47.090 --> 00:16:49.660
Yuzu would try to stop me!

00:16:49.660 --> 00:16:50.510
Miou...

00:16:55.300 --> 00:16:56.660
Do you have feelings for Yuzu?

00:16:58.060 --> 00:16:59.020
I'm done.

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:01.550
I'm tired of going in circles and waiting.

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:05.180
I feel so lame.

00:17:06.100 --> 00:17:06.990
Miou?

00:17:07.530 --> 00:17:10.470
Yuzu gave me these earrings.

00:17:11.470 --> 00:17:12.580
I don't need them anymore.

00:17:19.650 --> 00:17:20.540
Nino!

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:23.860
What are you doing, you idiot?!

00:17:23.860 --> 00:17:25.650
Your earrings will get washed away.

00:17:25.650 --> 00:17:28.610
There's no way you'll find 
them! It's fine, okay?!

00:17:28.800 --> 00:17:30.980
Is it really? You won't regret it?

00:17:32.450 --> 00:17:33.550
It's fine.

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:38.060
I told you, it's fine!

00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:40.820
That's enough. I've already given up!

00:17:45.930 --> 00:17:48.920
I'm not like you!

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:50.560
You know what?

00:17:50.560 --> 00:17:53.670
Most people wouldn't keep singing 
for someone for six years.

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:55.920
You're the weird one!

00:18:00.360 --> 00:18:01.430
I know that.

00:18:01.640 --> 00:18:03.180
I know that already!

00:18:04.570 --> 00:18:07.400
I sing here as loudly as I can every morning.

00:18:07.400 --> 00:18:09.670
I know that isn't normal!

00:18:09.670 --> 00:18:13.210
I've been laughed at and made 
fun of over and over again.

00:18:13.210 --> 00:18:16.280
I've more than gotten used to it by now!

00:18:16.750 --> 00:18:19.780
I know I'm weird, thanks! 
Got a problem with that?!

00:18:25.240 --> 00:18:26.390
Even I...

00:18:27.380 --> 00:18:30.050
sometimes thought singing
here was pointless.

00:18:30.050 --> 00:18:31.630
I thought about quitting all the time.

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:33.280
But...

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:37.880
You should quit only after 
you've gone as far as you can.

00:18:38.610 --> 00:18:40.640
That's why I'll sing.

00:18:41.060 --> 00:18:44.640
No matter how unseemly, 
stupid, or weird I look.

00:18:51.510 --> 00:18:53.740
Sorry, Miou. You're all wet.

00:18:53.740 --> 00:18:54.760
Let me dry—

00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:56.550
Miou.

00:18:57.020 --> 00:18:58.150
What?

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:01.270
One was stuck to my pocket.

00:19:02.210 --> 00:19:05.380
It's very tenacious, and it shines brightly.

00:19:05.380 --> 00:19:07.440
Just like you.

00:19:09.020 --> 00:19:09.920
How do they look?

00:19:10.140 --> 00:19:11.470
Really good!

00:19:11.470 --> 00:19:14.420
They were the ones that looked 
most like you in the store.

00:19:15.870 --> 00:19:18.940
Thanks. I'll always treasure them.

00:19:24.470 --> 00:19:26.430
My medicine's all soaked, too.

00:19:26.710 --> 00:19:28.430
Medicine for what? A cold?

00:19:28.700 --> 00:19:30.260
I don't know.

00:19:30.260 --> 00:19:34.820
My chest has been hurting since yesterday, 
when I heard Momo was living with a woman.

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:36.930
I'll go to a hospital for it tomorrow.

00:19:37.380 --> 00:19:40.450
You don't need to go. 
It's probably just jealousy.

00:19:40.680 --> 00:19:41.310
Huh?

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:44.810
Nino, aren't you just jealous of that woman?

00:19:46.790 --> 00:19:48.620
I... I am?!

00:19:49.260 --> 00:19:53.200
Nino, is this... the first time 
you've ever felt jealous?

00:19:53.200 --> 00:19:55.500
So this is jealousy.

00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:02.340
All right, do your best.

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:04.010
I'm expecting good work.

00:20:04.230 --> 00:20:05.510
Was that Yuzu-kun?

00:20:05.510 --> 00:20:08.980
Yep. Looks like we'll be able to get 
enough songs together for the album.

00:20:08.980 --> 00:20:10.210
But you know...

00:20:10.210 --> 00:20:11.390
Is something wrong?

00:20:11.660 --> 00:20:15.150
The release date of Kiryuu 
Momo's band's debut album

00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:17.580
is the same day as In NO 
Hurry's first album release.

00:20:17.970 --> 00:20:20.040
And not just that. Look at this band name.

00:20:20.040 --> 00:20:22.500
I can tell we're on their mind.

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:24.770
Wait, these guys...

00:20:22.910 --> 00:20:31.540
August 12th 
Rock Horizon Line-up Decided!!

00:20:24.770 --> 00:20:26.400
are performing at the Summer Festival?

00:20:26.400 --> 00:20:29.170
Oh, you mean Rock Horizon?

00:20:29.170 --> 00:20:30.010
Yeah.

00:20:30.010 --> 00:20:32.990
We got an offer to play there, too.

00:20:32.990 --> 00:20:33.880
Seriously?

00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:34.530
Yep.

00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:37.540
Yana-san, that face isn't flattering.

00:20:37.870 --> 00:20:42.170
It's my belief that you should accept 
and win any fight brought to you.

00:20:43.410 --> 00:20:44.630
Kanade?

00:20:46.400 --> 00:20:47.530
Kanade?

00:20:59.260 --> 00:21:00.070
<i>We all</i>

00:21:01.370 --> 00:21:06.070
<i>had our hearts full of these stupid, 
unseemly feelings that shone brightly.</i>

00:21:06.790 --> 00:21:09.330
You really are weird.

00:21:11.330 --> 00:21:12.710
I'll take that as a compliment.

00:21:17.100 --> 00:21:18.610
What's with that?

00:21:22.420 --> 00:21:23.730
<i>And we walk forward today.</i>

00:21:30.180 --> 00:21:34.060
<i>Oh, no. I wonder if I really do have a cold.</i>

00:21:35.010 --> 00:21:37.640
<i>And why is Yuzu so late?</i>

00:21:38.570 --> 00:21:42.300
<i>He's usually here before me...</i>

00:21:54.530 --> 00:21:56.720
You're not even an early riser.

00:21:59.220 --> 00:22:01.530
What are you doing here so early?

00:22:07.360 --> 00:22:08.750
<i>Today and tomorrow...</i>

00:22:10.400 --> 00:22:11.340
<i>Damn it.</i>

00:22:11.340 --> 00:22:12.240
<i>...we'll walk.</i>

00:22:12.240 --> 00:22:13.220
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:22:14.740 --> 00:22:15.940
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:23:47.110 --> 00:23:52.280
♭07 
Our Lines of Sight Finally Overlapped
